cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PTS-WFM4Cities, please cite this software and the associated article when available."
title: "PTS-WFM4Cities: progressive threshold scanning on DEM-inspired urban scalar surfaces"
abstract: "Construction of DEM-inspired urban scalar surfaces from point or grid
  data and their analysis with progressive threshold scanning (PTS): projected
  area A(h), normalised excess volume V(h), connected-component count N(h) and
  largest-component share L(h), through a library API, a command line and a
  bilingual desktop interface."
type: software
version: 3.1.22
date-released: 2026-10-15
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/zhangzuocughustccnu/PTS-WFM4Cities"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/PTS-WFM4Cities/"
keywords:
  - urban morphology
  - progressive threshold scanning
  - scalar surface
  - spatial analysis
  - point pattern
